From b748cec19685d6dd67542868fb785e8cfe120698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:22:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 524/526] [DS4.1] Names: the V4.1 cache layout and attention
 ops lose B12X's name

The V4.1 cache layout, metadata and builder classes kept B12X's name after
0493 (DeepseekV41B12x*); TileLang's backend subclasses them. With B12X
leaving the image:

- DeepseekV41B12xMetadata, DeepseekV41B12xMetadataBuilder and
  DeepseekV41B12xBackend become DeepseekV41Metadata,
  DeepseekV41MetadataBuilder and DeepseekV41Backend;
- the base backend reports "DSV41" (was "B12X") and the compressor's
  "DSV41_COMPRESSOR" (was "B12X_DSV41_COMPRESSOR"); TileLang's still
  reports "TILELANG";
- the caches' cache_dtype_str is "dsv41" (was "b12x_dsv41"), a label
  specs of one group must share, with the same bytes;
- the opaque ops are vllm::dsv41_attention and vllm::dsv41_prepare_global_kv.

Nothing outside the DS4.1 package and its tests named them. tilelang/
vision.py's docstring says the B12X kernels it matches are no longer
installed.
